Model spatial continuity without mistaking sampling patterns for geology (@mine-geostatistics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Geostatistical-Declustering-and-Variograms.lingua#r_1MDWJYNM88E34YCM4918C7DEEQ", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Estimation-simulation-and-resource-uncertainty.lingua#r_76YQYSAEDVHX9K3MRFYXAMKG9D") { r_10MVCKPNDF22PMZ7CT6MGP87N4
**Read:** [Geostatistical sampling, continuity, estimation, and simulation — Deutsch and contributors](../sources/Geostatistical-Declustering-and-Variograms.lingua#r_1MDWJYNM88E34YCM4918C7DEEQ), both named lessons in full and the complete individually identified method used; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the full relevant resource-estimation discussion; [Measurement and metrology](../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), sampling, dependence, uncertainty, and model checking as needed.

Spatially close observations can share information and errors, while preferential sampling can bias a simple global average. Declustering and continuity analysis address different questions: representative distributions, spatial dependence, and prediction need their own target, support, domain, and assumptions.

An experimental semivariogram summarizes squared differences over defined lag/direction groups under a chosen procedure. Nugget, range, sill, anisotropy, trend, support, and estimation uncertainty have model-specific meanings. A few pairs or an attractive fitted curve cannot uniquely establish subsurface continuity.

Domain stationarity and a variogram model are investigative assumptions, tested against geology, sampling and held-out information. Duplicate/prepared analyses may quantify a different contribution from field-scale variability. Changing support can change the variance and continuity account.

**Work:** read the full declustering and sill lessons and complete the exact prediction/simulation method selected for the study. Compare raw and declustered summaries with explicit parameters and origins. Construct directional continuity diagnostics, preserve pair support/counts, and test a geologically plausible alternative domain/trend interpretation.

Explain how a held-out design matches the intended prediction, such as a new area, depth, or support. The broader statistics/geostatistical methods can be studied further as needed; the mine-specific result must show how their assumptions affect a material quantity or decision rather than treating software defaults as observed geology.

**Continue:** [Distinguish a best estimate from possible realizations and a reporting category](Estimation-simulation-and-resource-uncertainty.lingua#r_76YQYSAEDVHX9K3MRFYXAMKG9D).

